	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "ex8wWZ8KfqZiMJuTb",
			"description": "Laspistol, Common Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The commonest sidearm in the Imperium: issued to Guard officers, Munitorum staff, hive militia and anyone who rates a weapon above a stub pistol. Depicted constantly across Black Library Guard fiction (Gaunt's Ghosts, the Ciaphas Cain novels) as the backup weapon of choice once a soldier's lasgun runs dry or their hands are full.\n\nDesign: Damage is the fixed laspistol anchor (3d(2) burn). Average roll 10.5 already kills an unarmoured man (HP 10) in 1-2 hits per framework.md; the (2) divisor is carried by every las weapon in the post-Rescale lineup so a laspistol still means something against flak (DR 12): 3d(2) penetrates 90.7% of hits there, but never against carapace (DR 45, effective 22.5) — 0% of hits get through. Acc, range, RoF and shot count are not anchored, so they're built from scratch for a hand-held energy pistol: a smaller accumulator than a lasgun's gives roughly half the lasgun's shot count (30 vs. 60), and the short emitter keeps Bulk and ST modest. RoF 3 represents the selector's rapid-pulse setting rather than a sustained full-auto mode.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "3",
			"base_value": "150",
			"base_weight": "2.5 lb",
