		{
			"id": "e38ToVKwUIras-fWj",
			"description": "Lasgun, Kantrael Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The most widely issued lasgun in the Astra Militarum, standard Departmento Munitorum pattern and the rifle carried by the Cadian shock troops in codex background and countless Black Library novels. Some Munitorum logistics texts refer to the same basic mass-production design as \"M-Galaxy pattern\"; this entry treats the two names as the same underlying weapon rather than asserting they're formally distinct.\n\nDesign: Damage is the fixed lasgun anchor (5d(2) burn). Range/RoF/shots are not anchored and are built to match the lasgun's lore signature: a 60-shot accumulator that recharges off almost any power source, and a fire selector giving single, burst and full-auto settings (abstracted here as RoF 10 for full-auto; treat single fire as RoF 1 at the GM's discretion). Required lasgun-vs-armour check (framework.md, exact dice distribution): 5d(2) averages 17.5 and penetrates flak (DR 12, effective 6) on 99.9% of hits, matching \"punches flak\"; against carapace (DR 45, effective 22.5) it penetrates only 9.8% of hits, matching \"penetrates carapace about one hit in ten\"; against Astartes power armour (DR 100, effective 50) it penetrates 0% of hits, matching \"useless against power armour.\" No departure from the anchor was needed — the numbers check out as written. The Hot-shot pack usage reuses the hellgun anchor (6d(3) burn) exactly, since a hot-shot pack is explicitly the same overcharge trick as a hellgun's power cell, just dropped into an ordinary lasgun for one shot. The Overcharge usage is a milder, non-hellgun field expedient stepped up from the lasgun anchor: +1 die (6d burn, average 21), no armour divisor, limited shots — it still only clears flak (98.0% of hits) and fails against carapace (0% of hits), because the whole point of the divisor is what an overcharge pack doesn't add.",
