			"id": "ec-QLUJ0NyxxDyD-8",
			"description": "Lasgun, Triplex Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Named for its three-position fire selector, the Triplex pattern adds a mechanical 3-round burst mode on top of the usual single/full-auto options found across the standard lasgun family.\n\nDesign: Damage fixed at the lasgun anchor (5d(2) burn) for both modes — the selector changes how the shots are grouped, not the lasing output. The controlled 3-round burst gets a +1 Acc bump over the full-auto line (7 vs. 6) to represent the tighter grouping a mechanical burst limiter gives compared to unrestrained full-auto fire.",
