		{
			"id": "eZDnzlI-JLkYF70cN",
			"description": "Long-Las",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A sniper-modified lasgun with an added focusing lens and a stabilised barrel; Gaunt's Ghosts' marksman Mad Larkin's long-las is the best known example, and the weapon recurs as the Guard's standard sniper tool across Black Library fiction.\n\nDesign: Damage is the fixed long-las anchor (6d(2) burn), one die over the standard lasgun — an extra focusing chamber concentrates more energy per shot at the cost of rate of fire, and keeps the same (2) divisor family-wide. Average roll 21 makes flak (DR 12) meaningless (100% of hits penetrate) and gets through carapace (DR 45, effective 22.5) on 36.3% of hits, comfortably better than the lasgun's 9.8% and matching the long-las's role as the harder-hitting sniper pattern; it still fails outright against Astartes power armour (0% of hits). RoF drops to 1 (no autofire mechanism survives the rebuild) and the custom cell holds fewer shots than a stock lasgun. Acc rises to 9 for the integral scope, and Bulk worsens to -6 for the longer, heavier weapon, following the usual GURPS convention for a dedicated sniper rifle.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "1200",
			"base_weight": "11 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
