		{
			"id": "eFnP3xPjtRy2_ffwz",
			"description": "Hellpistol",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A compact hot-shot sidearm issued alongside the hellgun to Militarum Tempestus officers and Inquisitorial agents who need a backup weapon that can still trouble carapace armour.\n\nDesign: Scaled from the hellgun anchor (6d(3) burn) the same way the laspistol steps down one die from the lasgun: -1d, armour divisor unchanged. The (3) divisor is what lets it beat carapace at all — that's the entire point of the hot-shot family, so it carries over unmodified. Average roll 17.5 against carapace (DR 45, effective 15) penetrates 69.5% of hits: a real threat, if less reliable than the full-size hellgun's 90.4%. Shot count is lower than an ordinary laspistol's because a hot-shot cell packs more energy per shot into the same volume, so it burns out faster.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Militarum Tempestus"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "2",
