		{
			"id": "eRtelhWXkujAhZk6c",
			"description": "Hellgun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The signature weapon of the Militarum Tempestus Scions, an overcharged lasgun-pattern rifle purpose-built to beat armour a standard lasgun can't; its role as the carapace-killer of Imperial small arms is consistent background across Scion-focused fiction and codex material.\n\nDesign: Damage is the fixed hellgun anchor (6d(3) burn) exactly. Sanity check against the framework's stated purpose, computed by exact dice distribution: average roll 21, armour divisor 3 cuts carapace's DR 45 to an effective 15, so 6d(3) penetrates carapace on 90.4% of hits — it reliably beats carapace, confirming \"built to beat carapace\" with no adjustment needed. Against Sororitas power armour (DR 70, effective 23.3) it still gets through 27.9% of the time; against Astartes power armour (DR 100, effective 33.3) that drops to 0.1%, essentially none, matching hellgun's place below the boltgun as an infantry-scale weapon. Shot count (40) is lower than a standard lasgun's 60 to reflect the hungrier, hotter cell; ST is bumped to 7 for the heavier housing needed to safely contain the higher-energy discharge.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Militarum Tempestus"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "1600",
			"base_weight": "9 lb",
